01:34.860 --> 01:36.570
My name is Asami.

01:36.570 --> 01:38.820
I'm a 17-year-old high school girl.

01:39.490 --> 01:43.290
I keep it secret from everyone, but...

01:43.290 --> 01:45.120
I'm actually married.

01:45.710 --> 01:50.840
My husband, Ichimaru Kyousuke-sensei,
teaches physics at my school.

01:52.920 --> 01:56.010
Oh, Darling, since we only have school for half the day on Saturdays,

01:56.010 --> 01:59.260
I was going to do some shopping on my way home.

01:59.260 --> 02:02.810
I need to get restocked
on summer supplies.

02:02.810 --> 02:04.970
Ah, feel free to do so.

02:04.970 --> 02:08.140
What style of shirt do you want?

02:08.140 --> 02:10.190
Umm, I'm not sure.

02:10.190 --> 02:11.690
Which color?

02:11.690 --> 02:13.980
Maybe I should
let you decide, Asami.

02:14.860 --> 02:18.030
Anything you choose
will be fine with me.

02:18.030 --> 02:19.200
Okay!

02:19.240 --> 02:24.160
My Husband Told a Lie...

02:25.500 --> 02:29.580
Okay, Hirataki-san, can you translate the part up to where we stopped?

02:29.580 --> 02:31.290
O-Okay.

02:32.040 --> 02:34.170
Umm, Aunt Dory was a twin...

02:34.170 --> 02:38.720
Hey, hey. Don't you think Iwasaki-san's looking really sexy today?

02:38.720 --> 02:40.430
She must have a new boyfriend.

02:40.430 --> 02:41.260
Huh?

02:41.260 --> 02:43.390
Women make changes to appeal to men.

02:43.760 --> 02:47.640
Iwasaki-sensei's a lot more serious
and mature than I gave her credit for.

02:47.640 --> 02:49.390
Who is chatting back there?

02:49.940 --> 02:51.650
Please keep quiet in class!

02:52.360 --> 02:53.650
Busted...

03:02.120 --> 03:05.450
Finally! I thought this week
would never end.

03:06.080 --> 03:07.620
Hey, wanna go sing karaoke?

03:07.620 --> 03:09.370
I can't; I have my club.

03:09.370 --> 03:11.710
It's okay to skip it
every now and then.

03:11.710 --> 03:12.960
What about you, Asami?

03:12.960 --> 03:15.090
I need to do some shopping.

03:15.090 --> 03:17.420
Shopping!? Sounds good, I'll come too.

03:17.420 --> 03:19.920
Can't you get your boyfriend
to go with you?

03:19.920 --> 03:22.010
Not when I dumped him
a few days ago.

03:22.010 --> 03:25.010
B-But I have important
errands to run, as well.

03:25.720 --> 03:27.060
B-Bye.

03:28.180 --> 03:29.430
Today?

03:30.180 --> 03:35.900
I was hoping you would
join me for tea again.

03:36.860 --> 03:38.820
Are you willing?

03:39.820 --> 03:42.610
I swear, it's just for tea.

03:43.070 --> 03:44.700
S-Sure...

03:49.200 --> 03:50.450
Darling?

03:51.080 --> 03:52.460
A-Asami!

03:55.790 --> 03:57.000
E-Excuse me.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.130
Goodbye.

03:58.130 --> 03:59.800
G-Goodbye.

04:03.840 --> 04:07.720
What was he talking about with Iwasaki-sensei?

04:12.480 --> 04:15.270
Which would look best on my husband?

04:18.860 --> 04:20.820
It's gotta be this one.

04:22.950 --> 04:24.860
Thank you very much.

04:26.320 --> 04:30.290
And now, I'd better get home and start preparing dinner.

04:31.370 --> 04:33.290
Asami~!

04:33.580 --> 04:34.870
W-What's up?

04:34.870 --> 04:36.250
We're going to karaoke now.

04:36.880 --> 04:38.000
You too, Kasumi?

04:38.000 --> 04:40.670
She hung around and waited for my club to let out...

04:40.670 --> 04:43.510
Wow, we got a big spender here!

04:45.720 --> 04:47.930
And aren't these <i>men's</i> clothes?

04:47.930 --> 04:49.760
So, who're they for?

04:49.760 --> 04:51.470
Just give them back already!

04:53.770 --> 04:54.560
Oww...

04:54.560 --> 04:56.730
They really are for men.

04:57.100 --> 04:59.770
D-Don't tell me it's for Ichimaru-sensei?!

04:59.770 --> 05:01.690
N-No, it's...

05:03.030 --> 05:04.740
Asami-oneechan!

05:04.740 --> 05:05.950
Sasuke-kun?!

05:05.950 --> 05:06.780
Aha!

05:08.070 --> 05:11.990
That shirt's... for your big brother, right?

05:11.990 --> 05:13.960
Umm, no, that's...

05:13.960 --> 05:15.460
"Your brother"?

05:16.120 --> 05:17.580
What brother?

05:17.580 --> 05:19.710
Weren't you an only child, Asami?

05:19.710 --> 05:21.130
You had an older brother?

05:21.130 --> 05:24.010
Oh, no, you see...

05:25.220 --> 05:27.390
C-Come over here, you two!

05:27.720 --> 05:28.890
Please...

05:29.260 --> 05:32.930
The fact that we're siblings is a secret at school.

05:40.310 --> 05:41.070
I get it.

05:42.230 --> 05:45.740
Everybody has something
they don't want made public.

05:46.110 --> 05:47.610
Thank you so much.

05:54.450 --> 05:56.960
Hey, Asami, what was that
about a brother?

05:56.960 --> 06:00.290
He sure is a sweet and good-looking guy.

06:00.290 --> 06:02.250
S-Sakura-san!

06:02.250 --> 06:05.510
That said, he's actually her cousin.

06:06.170 --> 06:07.220
Y-Yeah.

06:07.220 --> 06:08.550
"Cousin"?

06:08.550 --> 06:12.720
For some reason,
Asami chan refers to him as "Onii-chan."

06:08.800 --> 06:14.020
Note: In Japanese, terms for older siblings can also be used
for other relatives and older acquaintances/strangers.

06:12.720 --> 06:14.020
Oh, so that's it.

06:15.100 --> 06:17.390
Thank you, Sakura-san.

06:22.110 --> 06:25.860
I guess I'd better get going,
if I don't want to be late for work.

06:25.860 --> 06:28.490
Buh-bye, Asami-oneechan!

06:28.490 --> 06:30.110
By the way...

06:29.700 --> 06:31.200
Who <i>are</i> those two?

06:31.200 --> 06:32.870
My neighbors.

06:33.870 --> 06:37.370
Hey, Asami, are you done with your important errands?

06:37.370 --> 06:39.460
Y-Yes.

06:39.460 --> 06:40.960
Wanna do some karaoke?

06:41.460 --> 06:43.590
I'm sorry, but I have to go home.

06:43.590 --> 06:45.000
Huh?

06:58.520 --> 07:01.100
It's Ichimaru-sensei and Iwasaki-sensei.

07:01.560 --> 07:03.110
Darling...

07:05.190 --> 07:06.320
I see...

07:06.820 --> 07:09.700
Iwasaki-sensei has been acting sexier

07:09.700 --> 07:12.320
because she's dating Ichimaru-sensei.

07:13.200 --> 07:16.120
I suppose you can't really blame the guy.

07:16.120 --> 07:18.700
D-Don't go jumping to conclusions!

07:19.210 --> 07:21.830
Ichimaru-sensei isn't that sort of man.

07:23.460 --> 07:27.210
I know how you feel about him,
but you've got to know when to fold 'em.

07:27.590 --> 07:31.630
B-But it's normal for teachers
at the same school to have tea together.

07:31.630 --> 07:34.640
Yes, they're teachers and co-workers,

07:34.640 --> 07:36.930
so their having tea together
isn't unusual.

07:37.220 --> 07:40.940
But still, this is a Saturday evening
we're talking about.

07:41.390 --> 07:46.320
Would two teachers come all the way out here just to drink some tea?

07:49.740 --> 07:51.240
I'm...

07:52.570 --> 07:54.280
...going home.

07:57.490 --> 07:59.540
Asami!

08:02.710 --> 08:04.000
That has to be it.

08:04.000 --> 08:08.630
They're just fellow teachers,
having tea together as co-workers.

08:09.300 --> 08:11.010
It's "only tea."

08:13.590 --> 08:15.010
Umm...

08:15.010 --> 08:15.890
Yes?

08:16.890 --> 08:19.430
Are you okay with staying out this late?

08:19.430 --> 08:20.390
It's okay.

08:21.520 --> 08:24.480
Since when did "just tea" last for over two hours?

08:27.310 --> 08:29.110
I should be heading out.

08:29.110 --> 08:30.730
P-Please stay...

08:34.070 --> 08:35.240
...just a little longer.

08:36.240 --> 08:38.740
Can't we chat a little more?

08:39.870 --> 08:41.290
Please.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.630
Fine.

08:53.470 --> 08:55.840
Sensei, you live alone, right?

08:57.010 --> 08:59.930
Oh, no... I mean, yes.

08:59.930 --> 09:01.720
Thank goodness.

09:01.720 --> 09:04.640
So it doesn't matter <i>when</i> you get home, right?

09:04.640 --> 09:08.440
Technically, no, but I have to
get up early tomorrow.

09:08.440 --> 09:10.770
So I ought to be leaving.

09:11.110 --> 09:11.820
Okay?

09:16.610 --> 09:17.700
<i>No...</i>

09:18.740 --> 09:20.160
U-Umm...

09:24.040 --> 09:26.670
<i>This does </i>not<i> look good.</i>

09:26.670 --> 09:28.130
Sensei...

09:28.540 --> 09:31.800
Please, don't make me say any more.

09:33.130 --> 09:35.420
I don't want to be alone tonight.

10:03.740 --> 10:06.830
What is up with Iwasaki-sensei today?

10:07.460 --> 10:08.870
Maybe...

10:10.170 --> 10:11.590
...she likes me?

10:13.250 --> 10:15.380
No, that can't be it.

10:16.720 --> 10:18.220
I'm home.

10:19.470 --> 10:21.720
Welcome back, Darling!

10:21.720 --> 10:23.140
Do you want dinner now?

10:23.640 --> 10:25.310
S-Sorry.

10:25.310 --> 10:26.640
I've already eaten.

10:27.730 --> 10:29.190
Y-You have?

10:29.190 --> 10:30.480
Sorry.

10:35.570 --> 10:38.990
Darling, you shouldn't lie down there.

10:39.820 --> 10:41.660
The bath is all ready.

10:44.740 --> 10:46.830
Hey, Darling?

10:50.040 --> 10:51.920
Darling...

10:57.630 --> 11:00.630
S-Sorry, I was tired, so...

11:01.090 --> 11:02.640
...I nodded off.

11:03.970 --> 11:06.680
You have been acting oddly today.

11:07.270 --> 11:10.310
You come home at such a late hour,
without so much as calling me.

11:10.310 --> 11:12.690
I'm sorry, but you know how it is.

11:13.690 --> 11:17.360
I was... asked to do a little overtime.

11:20.950 --> 11:22.280
Yeah.

11:23.660 --> 11:25.660
I suppose that's not your fault.

11:32.210 --> 11:36.050
Okay then! I'll take my bath now!

11:45.430 --> 11:47.060
Darling...

11:48.640 --> 11:52.100
My husband told a lie...

12:11.910 --> 12:13.620
My name is Asami.

12:13.620 --> 12:15.920
I'm a 17-year-old high school girl.

12:16.500 --> 12:20.380
I keep it secret from everyone, but...

12:20.380 --> 12:22.130
I'm actually married.

12:24.220 --> 12:30.220
My husband, Ichimaru Kyousuke-sensei,
teaches physics at my school.

12:39.940 --> 12:41.320
Good morning.

12:41.320 --> 12:42.990
Morning.

12:49.740 --> 12:54.750
Can I Trust Him...?

12:55.460 --> 12:57.920
Let's say, for example...

12:58.500 --> 13:02.460
The same quasar emits two pulses of light.

13:01.210 --> 13:05.260
<i>Darling, why did you lie to me?</i>

13:02.460 --> 13:08.390
The gravitational lensing effect
sends them on different courses.

13:05.260 --> 13:08.390
You had tea with Iwasaki-sensei, and yet...

13:10.100 --> 13:14.180
In the long run, as the influence of the gravitational lens wanes,

13:10.310 --> 13:12.980
<i>You told me that you were doing overtime.</i>

13:14.180 --> 13:16.270
a time differential develops.

13:17.440 --> 13:20.770
Hey, Asami, wanna hang out somewhere?

13:22.990 --> 13:25.280
Everyone needs
a change of pace sometimes.

13:25.740 --> 13:26.530
Karaoke!

13:26.910 --> 13:27.740
Bowling!

13:28.280 --> 13:29.240
Video arcades.

13:30.740 --> 13:33.200
Sorry, I'm not in the mood.

13:35.540 --> 13:40.000
Seeing him with Iwasaki-sensei was a real shock for her.

13:40.750 --> 13:43.010
Eh? A drinking party?

13:43.380 --> 13:46.510
Yeah. Kind of an informal gathering for the younger teachers.

13:47.010 --> 13:51.510
It'll be four or five people,
like Sonoda-sensei, Iwasaki-sensei...

13:53.100 --> 13:56.730
So I hate to say it,
but I'll be dining out tonight.

13:57.190 --> 13:58.270
Sorry.

13:59.020 --> 14:03.320
Darling, I can<i> believe you... can't I?</i>

14:03.320 --> 14:07.110
Is it truly just a social outing?

14:22.840 --> 14:24.590
Well, I'm leaving.

14:24.590 --> 14:25.800
Goodbye.

14:28.260 --> 14:31.760
There's nothing going on between you and Iwasaki-sensei, right?

14:45.070 --> 14:46.490
What's the matter?

14:47.820 --> 14:51.450
Ah, nothing. Just... have a good day.

14:52.370 --> 14:54.080
S-Sure.

14:57.750 --> 14:59.080
Asami?

15:02.540 --> 15:05.090
We can't go to school like this.

15:05.460 --> 15:06.920
Sorry...

15:08.760 --> 15:10.300
Just a little longer.

15:11.970 --> 15:14.470
Let's stay like this a little longer...

15:21.520 --> 15:24.440
Umm, we'll miss the train.

15:26.730 --> 15:28.150
I'm sorry.

15:29.650 --> 15:30.900
It's okay.

15:30.900 --> 15:32.280
Bye.

15:32.280 --> 15:33.450
Goodbye.

15:46.920 --> 15:49.130
Darling...

15:49.800 --> 15:52.130
If you really love me,

15:52.130 --> 15:55.140
then please come home
as soon as you can.

15:55.760 --> 15:58.140
Assuming you do love me.

16:01.350 --> 16:03.900
I don't want to be alone tonight.

16:03.900 --> 16:07.480
I have a very bad feeling about this whole "gathering" thing.

16:10.610 --> 16:13.610
Cheers, everybody!

16:14.740 --> 16:16.370
Down the whole thing!

16:16.370 --> 16:20.500
Relax. If you get too drunk,
I'll take <i>real</i> good care of you.

16:25.830 --> 16:28.840
Way to chug it, Ichimaru-sensei!

16:28.840 --> 16:30.300
One more, one more!

16:33.050 --> 16:36.140
My husband has gone out drinking.

16:36.720 --> 16:39.560
I hope he gets back soon.

16:44.270 --> 16:47.440
I'm going to get a little fresh air.

16:47.440 --> 16:49.070
You drunk already?

16:49.070 --> 16:50.650
What a lightweight!

16:53.030 --> 16:55.030
Come on, open your mouth.

16:55.030 --> 16:58.080
Umm, I'm going to get a little fresh air too.

16:58.080 --> 16:59.990
Oh, Iwasaki-sensei!

17:04.330 --> 17:06.000
So refreshing...

17:06.000 --> 17:07.750
Ichimaru-sensei.

17:09.630 --> 17:12.010
I-Iwasaki-sensei!

17:13.090 --> 17:14.340
Umm...

17:15.010 --> 17:18.010
Do you mind if I join you?

17:18.010 --> 17:20.100
Um, what?

17:28.110 --> 17:30.440
Well, this<i> is awkward.</i>

17:31.320 --> 17:33.440
Oh, umm...

17:33.440 --> 17:36.110
I'm going back inside now.

17:36.110 --> 17:37.990
Say...

17:38.660 --> 17:42.120
Sensei, am I annoying?

17:42.120 --> 17:44.540
T-Tears?

17:44.540 --> 17:47.790
I can't help it...

17:48.580 --> 17:50.380
My feelings for you
are too strong.

17:51.000 --> 17:52.750
I can't stop myself...

17:51.960 --> 17:52.750
N-No...

17:53.800 --> 17:55.550
...from crying.

17:57.800 --> 18:00.300
I-Iwasaki-sensei!

18:04.180 --> 18:06.850
O-Ouch...

18:06.850 --> 18:08.190
You know...

18:09.310 --> 18:13.190
I really <i>do love you.</i>

18:14.150 --> 18:16.190
No way!

18:16.190 --> 18:20.700
W-Wait a minute.
Even if you tell me that,

18:20.700 --> 18:23.330
I-I can't...

18:24.080 --> 18:27.370
S-Sorry, I got carried away.

18:27.370 --> 18:31.590
But I truly do love you, Ichimaru-sensei.

18:31.590 --> 18:32.340
That's why-

18:32.340 --> 18:35.920
Y-You know, I really appreciate that you have feelings for me.

18:36.210 --> 18:38.720
So you see, uhh...

18:39.890 --> 18:42.550
I'm sorry. I'm such a...

18:43.100 --> 18:47.020
You have somebody else...
someone you love, right?

18:47.020 --> 18:49.900
Huh? Not exactly, but...

18:49.900 --> 18:52.020
I should've known you'd be taken.

18:55.320 --> 18:57.570
It's hopeless for me.

18:59.530 --> 19:02.030
D-Don't talk like that.

19:02.370 --> 19:04.530
Come on, let's get back to the bar.

19:04.530 --> 19:05.950
Ichimaru-sensei?

19:07.120 --> 19:11.920
I apologize for saying all this without even considering the consequences.

19:13.000 --> 19:16.550
That's just how you are, right?

19:17.380 --> 19:18.880
Sensei...

19:20.840 --> 19:23.800
Even though you've told me that you love somebody else...

19:24.350 --> 19:27.770
I just don't care.

19:44.660 --> 19:46.160
I'm home.

19:48.500 --> 19:50.330
Welcome back!

19:51.500 --> 19:52.960
Asami.

19:56.710 --> 20:00.420
I'm sorry I left you all alone.

20:03.300 --> 20:05.470
I'm so happy.

20:06.390 --> 20:10.480
You came home as early as you could.

20:11.270 --> 20:14.730
I thought you wouldn't be home until after midnight.

20:15.020 --> 20:16.440
Asami.

20:24.030 --> 20:26.030
Darling.

20:26.580 --> 20:29.540
Won't you eat some cherries with me?

20:31.960 --> 20:33.540
So, how was it?

20:34.750 --> 20:38.040
Was everybody there?

20:38.040 --> 20:40.050
You know, like Iwasaki-sensei?

20:41.300 --> 20:45.930
W-Why am I so flustered?
Should I be feeling guilty?

20:49.760 --> 20:55.060
It was just us ranting about our opinions on the educational system and stuff.

20:56.060 --> 20:57.940
I see.

20:58.730 --> 21:00.070
Of course it would be.

21:01.530 --> 21:02.780
I...

21:04.280 --> 21:08.280
...believe in you, Darling.

21:10.950 --> 21:13.160
Please... Kiss me.

21:20.590 --> 21:22.050
Okay.

21:26.800 --> 21:28.550
That's not fair.

21:30.510 --> 21:33.060
I'm repossessing these cherries.

21:33.430 --> 21:35.390
O-Okay, one kiss.

21:35.390 --> 21:37.600
That train's left the station!

21:41.440 --> 21:42.530
But...

21:42.900 --> 21:46.070
I'm satisfied with just this much.

21:46.530 --> 21:50.160
Because I am ever so happy.

21:50.780 --> 21:52.370
So...

21:53.790 --> 21:56.540
Good night, Darling.

22:15.980 --> 22:19.480
All I am is a kitten

22:15.980 --> 22:19.480
watashi wa koneko

22:19.480 --> 22:23.400
All for you, and yours alone

22:19.480 --> 22:23.400
anata hitori dake no

22:23.400 --> 22:30.280
A naive little kitten; I want you to raise me right.

22:23.400 --> 22:30.280
mijuku na koneko sodatete hoshii no

22:30.820 --> 22:34.330
Can't you grant me this simple wish for anything

22:30.820 --> 22:34.330
nozomareru koto no subete ni

22:34.330 --> 22:38.500
and every last thing that I desire?

22:34.330 --> 22:38.500
kotaete yukeru kana

22:38.500 --> 22:41.920
If you stare at me with those longing, hungry eyes,

22:38.500 --> 22:41.920
nagai me de mitete kuretara

22:41.920 --> 22:47.840
I'll make this scene hotter and hotter just for you

22:41.920 --> 22:47.840
dokidoki sasete itte ageru

22:47.840 --> 22:55.220
Your kisses are like love vitamins,
so give me more and more of them.

22:47.840 --> 22:55.220
ai no bitamin kiss motto choudai

22:55.220 --> 23:02.150
Wrapped inside your loving arms so tight,
I can sleep again tonight.

22:55.220 --> 23:02.150
itoshii ude no naka kyou mo nemuru no

23:02.770 --> 23:12.280
Forever and ever only yours; just a kitten of love.

23:02.770 --> 23:12.280
zutto anata dake no ai no koneko

23:29.010 --> 23:44.900
Preview

23:29.470 --> 23:31.220
Asami here.

23:31.220 --> 23:34.970
The slightest little thing
can give a person's secret away.

23:35.310 --> 23:38.020
But I want you to kiss me more.

23:38.020 --> 23:39.350
Kiss me harder.

23:39.770 --> 23:43.440
So, please love me lots next week too.
